# ---- Snow (1) -------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-08-22.  SNOW_DIVERGENCE_REGISTER.md §4 called this a hard
# prerequisite once S2b landed.  Seven defects (F1-F7) were fixed in the snow
# module against a corpus in which no deck had a [SNOWPACKS] section, so
# "14/14 unchanged" could not observe any of them.
#
# EXPECT THIS DECK TO MOVE on any snow-module change -- that is what it is
# for.  A snow round that leaves it byte-identical has either changed nothing
# reachable or is not exercising what it claims.  It also carries its own
# stored baseline with provenance under tests/parity/snow/baseline/, which is
# separate from this runner and stays that way.
#
# Cost: 8,641 routing steps, MEASURED at 0.30 s -- among the FASTEST decks
# here, not the slowest.  The "~15-24 s" this line used to claim came from
# snow/README.md and was never measured on a CLI build; see README.md §5 for
# the per-deck table.  The three sdm_fv_* decks are 96 % of the corpus.
tests/parity/snow/snow_parity.inp	KINWAVE + [SNOWPACKS] -- the only deck with snow, water in a pack, or areal depletion

# ---- Water age and heat (3) -----------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-08-22.  README.md §4 recorded 0 water-age and 0 heat decks after
# roughly fifteen rounds of building both, so "15/15 byte-identical" could
# observe neither.  Same hole the snow deck closed for [SNOWPACKS], and that
# deck found a real ledger defect on its first run.
#
# All three share one network -- S1 -> S2 -> J1 with S3 -> J1 direct -- so a
# difference between them is the CAPABILITY and not the model.  The cascade is
# there because run-on is where both age defects lived (A3, A4); S3 is the
# no-run-on control.  Generated: tests/parity/transport/gen_transport_parity.py.
#
# EXPECT THESE TO MOVE on any age or heat change, exactly as the snow deck
# moves on a snow change.  Attribute the movement; do not widen anything.
tests/parity/transport/age_legacy.inp	WATER_AGE ON with np=0, default solver -- age through the LEGACY CSTR mirror (A1b)
tests/parity/transport/age_ard.inp	the same body under QUALITY_SOLVER EULERIAN_ARD -- age as an ARD mesh row (A1a); the pair localises a movement to one engine
tests/parity/transport/age_lard.inp	the same body once more under QUALITY_SOLVER LAGRANGIAN -- age as the LARD segment row (X4); the TRIPLE localises a movement to one of three engines
tests/parity/transport/heat_parity.inp	pollutant + age + heat -- the only deck reaching the np+age+heat reported stride (D-UT10's seam); carries heat_parity.heat beside it
